NAME
    vibecommander - two-panel file manager (Norton Commander style)

SYNOPSIS
    vibecommander [DIRECTORY]

DESCRIPTION
    A text-mode file manager in the style of Norton Commander and
    Midnight Commander. Two panels browse two directories side by
    side; Tab picks which panel is active. Enter opens the entry
    under the cursor (a directory changes the panel there, a
    regular file opens in the built-in viewer), Left leaves to the
    parent directory. A letter typed jumps to the first entry that
    starts with it.

    The function keys run the file operations, as on a Commander:

      F1 help   F3 view   F4 edit   F5 copy
      F6 move   F7 mkdir  F8 delete F10 quit

    F4 edits in vedit, running it as a child process; the manager
    returns when the editor exits. F5 and F6 copy and move the
    selected file into the other panel's directory. F7 asks for a
    name and creates the directory, F8 deletes the entry after a
    yes/no confirmation.

KEYS
    Tab             switch the active panel
    Enter / Right   open the entry under the cursor
    Left            leave to the parent directory
    Up / Down       move the cursor
    Home / End      jump to the first / last entry
    Space           page the list down
    a..z 0..9 . _ - jump to the first entry starting with it
    F1 F3 F4 F5 F6 F7 F8 F10   the operations above
    Esc             quit

    A screen layout from bottom to top: the function-key bar on the
    last row, the status line with the selected entry's size above
    it, the two lists, and the panel titles with their paths.
